{"caller": "codex", "commit": "9d024378399e917a1821c2ac7b883e485ee99c51", "date": "2026-10-06T09:26:10+00:00", "exit": 0, "files": ["conformance/corpus.py", "conformance/freeze_corpus.py", "conformance/native_library.py", "conformance/native_record.py", "conformance/native_replay_report.py", "plans/20261006-native-replay-storage.status.md", "reviews/log.jsonl", "tests/test_native_replay_storage.py", "tools/check_resources.py"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T092610Z-9d024378#1", "line": 165, "path": "tests/test_native_replay_storage.py", "rule": "R11", "severity": "should", "text": "The `valid` case runs the real freezer CLI in a subprocess, where `check_resources` measures real free disk space, so the test fails on a host with less than 10 GiB free on the workspace, temporary or Nix-store filesystem (the other tests patch `shutil.disk_usage` for this reason). Fix: run the CLI through `main()` in-process with `shutil.disk_usage` patched, or skip the `valid` case with a clear reason when free space is below `MIN_FREE_BYTES`."}, {"id": "20261006T092610Z-9d024378#2", "line": 86, "path": "conformance/freeze_corpus.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "The new message says the receipt \"requires explicit storage outside {directory} and {output}\", which tells the user that the storage directory must be outside those directories, but the check requires the receipt path to be outside them and requires `--temporary-root` separately. Fix: give two clear requirements, for example \"Native replay receipt {storage_report} must be outside {directory} and {output}, and --temporary-root must be given; select a receipt path outside both directories\"."}], "id": "20261006T092610Z-9d024378", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "claude", "revision": "@-", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188eadd60", "R4": "ea7ca17539eb", "R5": "b8613a2d693b", "R6": "5600dce59aef", "R7": "0b68df581c57", "R8": "b4168359c60d", "R9": "5a69196344d0"}, "well_formed": true}
{"date": "2026-10-06T09:32:03+00:00", "finding": "20261006T092610Z-9d024378#1", "kind": "resolution", "outcome": "rejected", "reason": "The declared development environment requires at least MIN_FREE_BYTES (10 GiB) before expensive work. This real CLI check deliberately exercises that resource guard; insufficient space is a prerequisite failure that AGENTS requires us to report, rather than hide through a skip or mocked successful capacity. The small test does not materially consume the required budget."}
