{"caller": "codex", "commit": "452e432cecc13e62351edf3845ac2fdc995830ac", "date": "2026-10-06T12:49:13+00:00", "exit": 1, "files": ["docs/conformance-progress.md", "plans/20261006-native-replay-storage.status.md", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/README.md", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-0-ordinary.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-0-tmpfs.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-0.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-1-ordinary.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-1-tmpfs.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-1.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-2-ordinary.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-2-tmpfs.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/case-2.json.gz", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/linux/receipt.json", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/measure.py", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/sha256.json", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/snapshot.json", "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/validate.py", "reviews/log.jsonl"], "findings": [{"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#1", "line": 42, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/README.md", "rule": "R13", "severity": "must", "text": "The README links to `linux/full.json` and states the 4,376-case results from it, but the commit does not contain `linux/full.json` because `jj` refused to snapshot the 2.1 MiB file, so the full-run evidence is not in the commit. Fix: add `linux/full.json` to the commit (for example with `jj --config snapshot.max-new-file-size=2242637` or stored compressed as `full.json.gz`), and update the README, `sha256.json`, `validate.py` and `measure.py` to match."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#2", "line": 33, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/validate.py", "rule": "R11", "severity": "must", "text": "`validate.py` reads `linux/full.json` and its hash is in `sha256.json:12`, so on a checkout of this commit the documented check `validate.py --source-root ...` stops with `FileNotFoundError`. Fix: commit the file it reads (or its compressed form), then run the validator again on a clean checkout."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#3", "line": 101, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/measure.py", "rule": "R11", "severity": "should", "text": "The representative selection, the filesystem-type check and the receipt pass/fail logic in `measure.py` are new behavior, and no test covers them. Fix: move the selection into a pure function and add a short test that checks the selected cases and the tie-break against a small fixture list."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#4", "line": 119, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/measure.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "The required filesystem types `'ext4'` and `'tmpfs'` are literals inside `main`, while the other run bounds are named constants. Fix: define a named mapping, for example `EXPECTED_FILESYSTEM_TYPES = {'ordinary': 'ext4', 'tmpfs': 'tmpfs'}`, with a docstring, and use it in `main`."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#5", "line": 26, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/measure.py", "rule": "R1", "severity": "should", "text": "`SELECTION_POLICY` describes the selection rule only as text; the rule itself is written separately inside `main`, and no test links the two. Fix: put the rule in a named function whose docstring is the policy, and record that function's description in the receipt."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#6", "line": 44, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/validate.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "\"Full replay identities or binding completion differ\" does not say which of the twelve checks failed or what the user can do next. Fix: check each condition separately, give a message that names the field and the file, and say what to do (for example, select the original source or get the receipt again)."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#7", "line": 31, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/validate.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "\"Retained evidence bytes changed: NAME\" says what failed but not what the user can do next. Fix: add the next step, for example \"Restore the file from the commit that added it, or record new evidence in a new report directory\"."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#8", "line": 113, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/measure.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "\"Three deterministic representative cases are required\" does not say which input failed or what to do next. Fix: name the corpus path and how many authored cases and upstream source files it has, and tell the user to select a corpus with one authored case and two upstream source files."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#9", "line": 56, "path": "reports/20261006-native-replay-storage/measure.py", "rule": "R10", "severity": "should", "text": "\"Fresh native observations differ from frozen evidence\" does not name the case or the storage root, or say what to do next. Fix: include `record['name']` and `storage` in the message, and tell the user to compare the retained child output with the frozen record."}, {"id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c#10", "line": 80, "path": "plans/20261006-native-replay-storage.status.md", "rule": "R13", "severity": "should", "text": "The status file still says \"the new Linux paired/full execution evidence remain pending\", which contradicts the completed-run entries added below it in the same file. Fix: change that line to say that the Linux evidence is retained and only the review is still pending."}], "id": "20261006T124913Z-452e432c", "kind": "review", "reviewer": "claude", "revision": "@-", "rules": {"R1": "62d446279093", "R10": "638d8cbd1df8", "R11": "5de19cdbbbc1", "R12": "99f66579f467", "R13": "da0926dafb88", "R2": "e5e78fb2a52a", "R3": "4f9188